{"id":28044,"slug":"my-beautiful-laundrette","title":"My Beautiful Laundrette","year":1985,"country":"United Kingdom","duration":98,"spine":767,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28044-my-beautiful-laundrette","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/17f96f9413ad320378ac50cede624921/tLddExzFtpz7o13GYWsutsVfFGrWiq_large.jpg","description":"Stephen Frears was at the forefront of the British cinematic revival of the mid-1980s, and the delightfully transgressive My Beautiful Laundrette is his greatest triumph of the period. Working from a richly layered script by Hanif Kureishi, who was soon to be an internationally renowned writer, Frears tells an uncommon love story that takes place between a young South London Pakistani man (Gordon Warnecke), who decides to open an upscale laundromat to make his family proud, and his childhood friend, a skinhead (Daniel Day-Lewis, in a breakthrough role) who volunteers to help make his dream a reality. This culture-clash comedy is also a subversive work of social realism that dares to address racism, homophobia, and sociopolitical marginalization in Margaret Thatcher’s England.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Stephen Frears","slug":"stephen-frears"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Saeed Jaffrey","role":"Nasser","slug":"saeed-jaffrey"},{"actor":"Roshan Seth","role":"Papa","slug":"roshan-seth"},{"actor":"Daniel Day-Lewis","role":"Johnny","slug":"daniel-day-lewis"},{"actor":"Gordon Warnecke","role":"Omar","slug":"gordon-warnecke"},{"actor":"Derrick Branche","role":"Salim","slug":"derrick-branche"},{"actor":"Shirley Anne Field","role":"Rachel","slug":"shirley-anne-field"},{"actor":"Charu Bala Chokshi","role":"Bilquis","slug":"charu-bala-chokshi"},{"actor":"Souad Faress","role":"Cherry","slug":"souad-faress"},{"actor":"Rita Wolf","role":"Tania","slug":"rita-wolf"},{"actor":"Richard Graham","role":"Genghis","slug":"richard-graham"},{"actor":"Gurdial Sira","role":"Zaki","slug":"gurdial-sira"},{"actor":"Stephen Marcu